<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila says to look into reports of smuggled meat.</title>
<headline>Manila says to look into reports of smuggled meat.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine Agriculture secretary Salvador Escudero said on Thursday the government will check on complaints by local meat processors the country was flooded by smuggled canned meat products.</p>
<p>&quot;If it can be proven that the products were smuggled, then we will seek assistance from police agencies,&quot; Escudero told reporters.</p>
<p>The Philippine Association of Meat Processors Inc (PAMPI) said it expected smuggled canned products this year to reach three million cases with a wholesale value of $75 million.</p>
<p>PAMPI has asked President Fidel Ramos to penalise local retailers selling smuggled canned meat products.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
</text>
